<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.14.3: Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01503</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.14.3: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>771ffe71-4fa6-4720-ba14-feb4c2b81cc8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Terence looked down the second column of the table below and noticed that \(\frac{3}{1}=\frac{9}{3}=\frac{27}{9}=\frac{81}{27}\). Because of his observation, he claimed that the input-output pairs in this table could be modeled with an exponential function. Explain why Terence is correct or incorrect. </para>
<table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        \(x\)
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        \(T(x)\)
      </entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        0
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        4
      </entry>
      <entry>
        9
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        13
      </entry>
      <entry>
        27
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        40
      </entry>
      <entry>
        81
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
</section>
</content>
</document>
